From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rudi Heitbaum <rudi@heitbaum.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 21:45:00 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/rockchip: vop: reject AFBC wider than the decoder can
 scan out

The AFBC decoder is programmed with hreg_block_split hardcoded to 0, so
SPLIT mode is never used. As the comment above ROCKCHIP_AFBC_MOD already
notes, SPLIT "could be enabled via the hreg_block_split register, but is
not currently handled".

Without it the decoder cannot keep a wide scanout fed. On rk3399 a 1920
wide AFBC framebuffer is displayed correctly while a 3840 wide one is
not displayed at all: the screen stays black.

Nothing catches this. vop_plane_atomic_check() validates the AFBC
format, the source offset and the rotation, but not the width, so the
atomic commit succeeds and the frame is silently lost. Userspace has no
way to tell that the configuration it asked for cannot work, and no
reason to fall back to a linear buffer.

Reject AFBC above the width the decoder can sustain, so the commit fails
and userspace falls back to linear instead of displaying nothing.

Tested on a Radxa ROCK Pi N10 (rk3399pro): with this applied a 4K
desktop is displayed instead of a black screen.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop.c | 7 +++++++
 drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop.h | 8 ++++++++
 2 files changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop.h b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop.h
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop.h
@@ -33,6 +33,14 @@
 			| AFBC_FORMAT_MOD_YTR \
 	)
 
+/*
+ * Without SPLIT mode the AFBC decoder cannot keep a wide scanout fed, so a
+ * wider framebuffer is displayed as a black screen. Reject it in the atomic
+ * check so that userspace falls back to a linear buffer rather than
+ * committing something that never appears.
+ */
+#define ROCKCHIP_AFBC_MAX_WIDTH		2560
+
 enum vop_data_format {
 	VOP_FMT_ARGB8888 = 0,
 	VOP_FMT_RGB888,
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop.c
@@ -883,6 +883,13 @@
 				      new_plane_state->rotation);
 			return -EINVAL;
 		}
+
+		if (drm_rect_width(&new_plane_state->src) >> 16 > ROCKCHIP_AFBC_MAX_WIDTH) {
+			DRM_DEBUG_KMS("AFBC is limited to %d pixels without SPLIT mode, width=%d\n",
+				      ROCKCHIP_AFBC_MAX_WIDTH,
+				      drm_rect_width(&new_plane_state->src) >> 16);
+			return -EINVAL;
+		}
 	}
 
 	return 0;
-- 
2.53.0
